# =============================================================================
# TEST 124 — AKBASCORE DRA 3.0
#
# ANGLE-CONTROLLED TRANSPORT CARTOGRAPHY
# DOES LOCAL FINITE RESPONSE PREDICT TERMINAL TRANSPORT
# AFTER CONTROLLING FOR SEMANTIC DISTANCE FROM THE SEED?
#
# Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct · BF16 · A100
#
# =============================================================================
#
# MOTIVATION
# ----------
#
# TEST123:
#
#   probe-selected vs cloud-random D19 = +0.011674
#   probe/terminal advantage corr      = +0.531768
#
# BUT:
#
#   selected angle:
#       5°  -> 26/40
#       10° -> 11/40
#       15° ->  2/40
#       20° ->  1/40
#       30° ->  0/40
#       45° ->  0/40
#
# Therefore TEST123 could not cleanly distinguish:
#
#   genuine transport information
#
# from:
#
#   preference for candidates close to the semantic seed.
#
#
# =============================================================================
# TEST124 QUESTION
# =============================================================================
#
# At a FIXED angular distance from the semantic seed:
#
#       does the tiny L11 -> L12 finite-response score T
#
# predict:
#
#       full-strength terminal D19 ?
#
#
# =============================================================================
# CORE DESIGN
# =============================================================================
#
# Six frozen angular shells:
#
#       5°, 10°, 15°, 20°, 30°, 45°
#
# Four random orthogonal deviations per shell.
#
#       6 shells × 4 candidates = 24 candidates / prompt
#
# For EVERY candidate:
#
#   PHASE A
#       tiny probe at L11
#       observe ONLY L12
#
#       G = ||delta12|| / ||probe11||
#
#       A = cos(delta12, v12)
#
#       T = G * A
#
#   PHASE B
#       apply SAME candidate at normal frozen DRA magnitude
#       measure D12, D13, D15, D19, P...
#
#
# IMPORTANT:
#
# All 24 candidates are evaluated terminally.
#
# Therefore TEST124 is a SYSTEM-IDENTIFICATION / CHARACTERIZATION assay.
# It is NOT a blind production-selection test.
#
# No candidate is tuned from D19 before its D19 measurement.
#
#
# =============================================================================
# PRIMARY ANALYSIS
# =============================================================================
#
# WITHIN EACH PROMPT × ANGLE SHELL:
#
#   4 candidates have exactly the same angle to seed.
#
# Therefore seed-distance is controlled.
#
# Primary metric:
#
#   within-shell centered correlation:
#
#       corr(
#           T_i - mean_shell(T),
#           D19_i - mean_shell(D19)
#       )
#
# pooled across all prompt-angle shells.
#
#
# This removes between-angle differences.
#
#
# =============================================================================
# SECOND PRIMARY DIAGNOSTIC
# =============================================================================
#
# Within each shell:
#
#       argmax(T)
#
# versus
#
#       mean(other 3 candidates)
#
# terminal D19.
#
# If the probe contains useful transport information:
#
#       D19[argmax(T)] > mean D19[others]
#
#
# =============================================================================
# ORACLE DIAGNOSTIC
# =============================================================================
#
# For characterization only:
#
#       argmax(T) vs argmax(D19)
#
# hit rate.
#
# Random expectation with 4 candidates = 25%.
#
# This is descriptive, not a p-value.
#
#
# =============================================================================
# FIXED SEED REFERENCE
# =============================================================================
#
# Original v11 is also evaluated once per prompt.
#
# This tells us how each angular shell compares with the original seed.
#
#
# =============================================================================
# PREDECLARED INTERPRETATION
# =============================================================================
#
# If within-shell centered T↔D19 correlation > 0
# AND top-T candidate has positive terminal advantage over shell peers:
#
#       ANGLE_CONTROLLED_TRANSPORT_SIGNAL_SUPPORTED
#
# If these disappear after angle control:
#
#       TEST123_SIGNAL_LARGELY_ANGLE_CONFOUNDED
#
# Otherwise:
#
#       ANGLE_CONTROLLED_SIGNAL_INCONCLUSIVE
#
#
# IMPORTANT:
#
# No Jacobian claim.
# No derivative claim.
# No manifold claim.
# No physical energy/momentum claim.
# No behavioral efficacy claim.
# No semantic-causality claim.
#
# =============================================================================


